{"name":"Brick Red","hex":"#8f1402","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"brick red","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A warm brownish-red colour similar to that of red clay bricks."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a warm brownish-red colour similar to that of red clay bricks."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/brick_red"}],"entries":[{"title":"Shades of red","blocks":[{"text":"Varieties of the color red may differ in hue, chroma, lightness, or in two or three of these qualities. Variations in value are also called tints and shades, a tint being a red or other hue mixed with white, a shade being mixed with black. A large selection of these various colors is shown below."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/3c/Shades_of_Red.svg/330px-Shades_of_Red.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shades_of_red","wikidata":"Q7460345"},{"title":"Brick","blocks":[{"text":"A brick is a type of building material used to build walls, pavements, and other elements in masonry construction. Properly, the term brick denotes a unit primarily composed of clay, but it is now also used informally to denote building units made of other materials or other chemically cured construction blocks."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/01/Brick.jpg/330px-Brick.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brick","wikidata":"Q40089"},{"title":"Red","blocks":[{"text":"Red is the color at the long wavelength end of the visible spectrum of light, next to orange and opposite violet. It has a dominant wavelength of approximately 625–750 nanometers. It is a primary color in the RGB color model and a secondary color in the CMYK color model, and is the complementary color of cyan. Reds range from the brilliant yellow-tinged scarlet and vermillion to bluish-red c